   "subject": "Retrieving client's time zone and date",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear all,<br><br>I&#39;m struggling with the client&#39;s time zone retrieval. This I&#39;d like to use it to timestamp some of the files my shiny app creates. This timestamp makes only sense with the client&#39;s data, and not with the server&#39;s.<br><br>I read that this information can be retrieved with javascript [1], but I see that the current shiny.js [2] already has some procedures to fetch this (for instance, within dateInputBindings there is a <span>getUTCDate</span>()).<br><br>Unfortunately I don&#39;t understand javascript and I don&#39;t see how to link this js chunk with the server.R. Any ideas of how to solve this?<br><br>Thank you in advance!<br><br>Isabel Martinez<br><br>[1] <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/24842229/how-to-retrieve-the-clients-current-time-and-time-zone-when-using-shiny\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/24842229/how-to-retrieve-the-clients-current-time-and-time-zone-when-using-shiny&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399049232000&amp;usg=AOvVaw304vqJRkeTfufIAjtnZco3\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/24842229/how-to-retrieve-the-clients-current-time-and-time-zone-when-using-shiny</a><br>[2] <a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/blob/5a9c4ad8f35a42addc336b1ddf7683fa293d65a2/inst/www/shared/shiny.js\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/blob/5a9c4ad8f35a42addc336b1ddf7683fa293d65a2/inst/www/shared/shiny.js&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399049232000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1fnpiLJBGpPdJ96CIlyNrl\">https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/blob/5a9c4ad8f35a42addc336b1ddf7683fa293d65a2/inst/www/shared/shiny.js</a><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "xJFzxr5hcK8J",
   "from": "Huidong TIAN",
   "author": "68ce5dd269fd758c",
   "date": "2015-04-24T14:42:02Z",
   "subject": "Re: Retrieving client's time zone and date",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">If you don&#39;t know JavaScript, learn it. Without JavaScript you can&#39;t go very far with Shiny, I think.<div><br></div><div>To your question: </div><div><br></div><div>1. create a textInput with id, e.g. #clientTime.</div><div>2. load this JavaScript in ui.R</div><div><div>$(document).ready(function(){</div><div>    var d = new Date();</div><div><div>    var target = $(&quot;#clientTime&quot;);</div><div>    target.val(d.toLocaleString());</div><div>    target.trigger(&quot;change&quot;);</div></div><div><br></div><div>});</div></div><div><br></div><div>3. add the following  in server.R</div><div>  observe({</div><div>  write( paste( Sys.time(), input$clientTime, sep = &quot;; &quot;), file = &quot;Data/clientTime.txt&quot;)</div><div>  })</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Tell me if it works. </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Friday, April 24, 2015 at 4:22:18 PM UTC+2, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ismart...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear all,<br><br>I&#39;m struggling with the client&#39;s time zone retrieval. This I&#39;d like to use it to timestamp some of the files my shiny app creates. This timestamp makes only sense with the client&#39;s data, and not with the server&#39;s.<br><br>I read that this information can be retrieved with javascript [1], but I see that the current shiny.js [2] already has some procedures to fetch this (for instance, within dateInputBindings there is a <span>getUTCDate</span>()).<br><br>Unfortunately I don&#39;t understand javascript and I don&#39;t see how to link this js chunk with the server.R. Any ideas of how to solve this?<br><br>Thank you in advance!<br><br>Isabel Martinez<br><br>[1] <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/24842229/how-to-retrieve-the-clients-current-time-and-time-zone-when-using-shiny\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/24842229/how-to-retrieve-the-clients-current-time-and-time-zone-when-using-shiny&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399049233000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0F3y1XTL96AahAppInejru\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/24842229/how-to-retrieve-the-clients-current-time-and-time-zone-when-using-shiny</a><br>[2] <a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/blob/5a9c4ad8f35a42addc336b1ddf7683fa293d65a2/inst/www/shared/shiny.js\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/blob/5a9c4ad8f35a42addc336b1ddf7683fa293d65a2/inst/www/shared/shiny.js&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399049233000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ISOsv3yMLjyuMJZUIkk-S\">https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/blob/5a9c4ad8f35a42addc336b1ddf7683fa293d65a2/inst/www/shared/shiny.js</a><br></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
