     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thank you very much.<br><br>Unfortunately when I do either of your recipes I get the value of the textInput and not the date.<br><br>Actually I have an HTML UI and therefore what I have done is:<br><br>First, to include either the Chang&#39;s or the Tian&#39;s snippet in the HTML preamble (for the sake of brevity I&#39;ll copy only one)<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">&lt;script</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;text/javascript&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#008\">&gt;</span></div></code></div></div>"
